OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,$A(W)
OL,3,GNEWSACould the ear replace the
OL,4,Afingertip for oxygen monitoring?
OL,5,
OL,6,FPulse oximeters work by sending light
OL,7,Fwaves through a patient's skin to
OL,8,Festimate the level of oxygen in the
OL,9,Fblood, but it has been found that the
OL,10,Flight can behave differently depending
OL,11,Fon skin tone.
OL,13,FA study at University Hospitals
OL,14,FBirmingham is now researching a new
OL,15,Fdevice designed to tackle the problem
OL,16,Fand hopes to find the solution inside
OL,17,Fthe ear.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
